WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.102
- It's always young
people that have,

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.603
that their frontal,

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:08.375
well, A, they have all of this
energy, all of this passion,

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they want to change
the world, right?

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.811
I mean, you talk
about young people

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:15.081
and always talking about
the want cultural change,

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.750
they want a revolution,
and they want to be part

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.251
of something bigger
than themselves.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.688
A lot of the older
folks, I'm 50 now,

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:25.592 align:start size:88% position:13%
we have gray hair, which
is a sign of wisdom.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.260
We've been around a while to see

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
that all this history stuff
is actually important.

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:33.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so when you're
young, you need a vision.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:37.804
And so I think that
if we give the vision

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.672
as older wiser people

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.941 align:start size:88% position:13%
who understand that
ideas have consequences,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.778
that history can teach us about

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.546 align:start size:81% position:19%
where we're headed
in the future,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:97% position:3%
that if they get on board with
that, and they're inspired,

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:55.155 align:start position:0%
if they catch the vision that's
rooted in the right stuff,

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.892
I think that that not only,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.126
I don't think that it's they

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are going to
make the difference.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:05.965
I'm banking on the power of
God working in their hearts

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.835
and through their minds
to make better decisions

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:11.504
than we've made in
this generation.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.672
That's where my hope is.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.075
(calm music)

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.147 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
is an '80s sit-com
legend, a touring speaker,

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.486 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
bringing the gospel
across America,

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.388
and the host of the
"Campfire Revival"

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.623
on Facebook and Instagram.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.626
Kirk, Cameron, welcome
to "The Rubin Report."

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.728
- Hey, Dave, it's so good
to be talking with you.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.896 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I hope you don't
mind me bringing you

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.131 line:0%
into my backyard like this.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.599 line:0%
I just thought it might
be a little different

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.234 line:0%
for your program
and the viewers.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Kirk, I believe this
is the first time,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.272
in I don't know, man, how
many hundreds or thousands

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.808
of shows that I've done that
someone has done it outdoors

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.977
with a fire and
an American flag.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:53.313
I've never been prouder.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:56.282 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You know, I just feel like
we got to go grassroots.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.817
We got to get real.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.919
And it's just, this is as
real as it gets for me.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
I got my tomato garden
off to the left.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got a fire here, s'mores
in a couple of hours.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:07.160
And you know, we're going to
play like "Born in the USA"

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.829
with the flag waving in the
breeze here pretty soon.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.998
- Are you allowed to
have an American flag

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:14.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
just waving in the breeze
in crazy California?

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.536 align:start size:81% position:19%
I don't want to
out you my friend,

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:21.541 align:start position:0%
but you are in crazy
California, not too far from me.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.144
- Well, I spend enough
time in Florida and Texas

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:27.046
and Tennessee to kind
of balance it out.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.816
So, I love it out here though.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.851
You know, it's a
beautiful state,

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.587
and it's my hope and my prayer

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:37.123
that good people
across this state

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:41.394 align:start size:88% position:13%
will begin to reclaim
the values that we want.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.630
And we want to see them
represented in this state

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.098
and not abandon it.

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.566
- Alright, well, we're going
to get to some of those values,

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.468
we're going to get to
that flag behind you,

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.170
and we're going to get to
the campfire and all that.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.639
But I got to start
at the beginning.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:56.342
And the beginning, for
us, is the eighties.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.510
You were on ""Growing Pains."

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.912
It was like the number one show

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.113
for a couple of years at least.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.614
How many seasons
was it on total?

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:04.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I believe we were on six
or seven seasons, yeah.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.219
- Six or seven seasons.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.921
Definitely number
one at some point.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:11.257
ABC, I remember eight
o'clock, Kirk Cameron,

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.458
""Growing Pains."

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.960
- Were you watching
as a little kid?

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, be honest, did you
stay up late and watch?

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I was not only
watching as a little kid,

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.898
but I did my research.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.600
So the show came out in '85,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.335 align:start size:81% position:19%
I was about eight,
nine years old,

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:25.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
and there was a belief
in my high school,

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
I grew up in Syosset
in Long Island,

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start position:0%
and we knew that "Growing Pains"
took place in Long Island.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.811
There was a rumor, it
took place in Syosset,

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:35.081
but we discussed this once
when I met you off-camera.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.283
You actually told me it
took place one town over.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.117
Is that correct?

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.520
- It took place in

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.988 align:start size:88% position:13%
Huntington, Long Island.
- One town over,

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.456
one town over.

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.792 align:start size:97% position:3%
- One town over on a street
called Robin Hood Lane.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.193 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't know if
that's a real street.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.428
- We had a Robbins Lane.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:51.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
We had a Robbins
Lane where I grew up.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.733
- Okay, well that
was in Syosset.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.802
Maybe in Huntington,
it was Robin Hood Lane.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.070
I don't know.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.973
- Well, anyway, you were
on a show that, to me,

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.975
like sort of just captured
what my childhood was like.

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:03.943 align:start size:97% position:3%
And, you know, you're a
couple of years older than me,

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.712 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we were basically
the same age.

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:09.015
My demeanor was very much
the demeanor of Mike Seaver

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:11.584
on that show, kind
of happy go lucky,

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:14.787 align:start size:97% position:3%
sort of popular or
whatever, that whole thing.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.824
You were a star at
a pretty young age.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:18.992
What was that like?

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.296
- Well, you know,
when I look back,

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.031
I have kids now, so
I have six children,

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.933
and I look back
and I think, man,

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.235
I would never want them
to be in the environment

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:32.705 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I was in, just
because it's so precarious.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.173
It's so dangerous.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.109 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, how many child TV
stars do you see that grow up,

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:38.177 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they turn out with their
head on their shoulders,

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:41.514
and, you know, where they're
not in jail, or they're not,

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:46.519
you know, just jumping off
some crazy cliff in some way?

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.522
And I think, wow, for me,
it was my only normal.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.658
I can't compare it to
a different childhood.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:54.160
And fortunately, I had
good people around me,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.396
but yeah, it was very strange

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.431 align:start size:97% position:3%
at 14 years old, people
asking me for my autograph.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.699
I thought, are you kidding?

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:00.900
This is some kind of a joke.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.402
But then it went on and on,

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:05.505
and, you know, it was
a crazy adventure,

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:10.510
but one that was beautiful,
I'm thankful, I met my wife,

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.179
I got to work on projects
that I'm passionate about

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.348
all because of "Growing Pains."

00:05:15.348 --> 00:05:18.284
And I just want to be a good
steward of these opportunities

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:19.719
in the platform now,

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:23.823
rather than just taking
advantage and, you know,

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.224
looking out for me.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:28.728 align:start position:0%
- So you met your wife, Chelsea,
29 years ago on the set?

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:30.163
Is that right, on the set?

00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:32.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
- We're going to celebrate
30 years this year.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.701 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I married Mike
Seaver's girlfriend.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.903 align:start size:88% position:13%
So you may remember
that beautiful brunette

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.706
who showed up on the
set because I sure do,

00:05:39.706 --> 00:05:42.508
and interestingly, I
actually met her first

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:45.645 align:start size:97% position:3%
on my sister, Candice
Cameron's, show "Full House."

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:49.215
And a year later, she showed
up as Mike Seaver's girlfriend,

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.651
and then I stole her
away from Mike Seaver

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:55.588
behind the scenes,
and I married her,

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.990 align:start position:0%
and we're going to be
celebrating 40 years this year.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.492
- That's hilarious.

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
You stole her from Mike
Seaver, who you also were.

00:06:01.461 --> 00:06:02.295
That's very deep.

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:03.496
That's very deep.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:05.465
- He didn't deserve her.

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:06.499
Not at all.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:07.433
No, no, no.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.901
- He was a goof ball, that guy.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, he always saw
too many fish in the sea.

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:13.106
He was playing in the field.

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:14.073
I was like, no.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.641
I'm a one-woman guy.

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:19.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I moved in, and I
managed to make her laugh

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:22.782 align:start size:84% position:16%
the first time I
kissed her on screen,

00:06:22.782 --> 00:06:26.586
and that was way ahead of
our real life relationship.

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:29.122 align:start size:88% position:13%
In the show, I actually
had to kiss her.

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:31.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mike Seaver had to kiss
her, and I made her laugh.

00:06:31.758 --> 00:06:33.993 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think that was the
charm that set the hook,

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.595
and now she's mine.

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:36.829
- And here we are.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.065
And you guys did all
the serious stuff.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:41.267
You know, the eighties had
their melancholy episodes.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was the episode
where you and your friends

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:46.305
went to that party, and a
bunch of them did cocaine,

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:48.908
but Mike did not.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:49.742
And you've grown up to be-

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.077
- Say no to blow.

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.011
- Yeah.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:52.845
(Dave chuckling)

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:54.080
- That's what it was.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.014 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And you've grown up
to be a good family man.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.250
Six freaking kids, that's nuts.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.451
- Well, it is.

00:06:58.451 --> 00:06:59.385
You know, unless
you're the Duggars,

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:00.686
then that's just light work.

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:03.356 align:start size:88% position:13%
But it's been, you
know, it's kind of like

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.590
the "Brady Bunch."

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.794
I don't have Alice the
maid or Sam the butcher,

00:07:07.794 --> 00:07:10.496
but we got a house full of kids.

00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:11.364
It's been awesome.

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.632
They're grown now.

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:16.536
So my kids are now 23,
22, 21, 20, 19 and 18.

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:19.105 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so I've got
proposals and marriages.

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:21.941
I've got college
and graduations.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:23.876 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so we're just
kind of dealing with

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:25.111
the gamut of it right now.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:28.147
And it's always a
growing experience,

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:30.483 align:start size:84% position:16%
not just for them,
but for us as parents.

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:33.286
- Are you saying there are
growing pains involved, Kirk?

00:07:33.286 --> 00:07:34.520
- I am, I am.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.155
But I wanted you
to say it, not me.

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:36.989
(both chuckling)

00:07:36.989 --> 00:07:38.224
So thank you.

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:39.926
- So talk to me a
little bit about

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:43.429
the show ends, and
then eventually you
kind of reappeared,

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:45.531 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you started talking
more about faith

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.400
and the things that
mattered to you.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.001
And then the media was kind of

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:50.603
not that nice about it, right?

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:53.539 align:start size:84% position:16%
Or did that take a
little while at first?

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:54.373
- It was good.

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:55.575
You know what?

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:57.844 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was good fodder
for the tabloid shows.

00:07:57.844 --> 00:07:59.245
It was good ratings stuff.

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:02.782 align:start size:97% position:3%
But in reality, what happened
was I was an atheist.

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:06.986 align:start size:88% position:13%
I was one of many people
who just, you know,

00:08:06.986 --> 00:08:09.922 align:start position:0%
never really thought about
God, never thought about faith.

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:11.524
I had more faith in
myself, you know,

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:14.160
or people that I looked up to.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then one day, a pretty
young girl invited me

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:20.299
to meet her family and
they went to church.

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:21.667
And so I was an atheist,

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so I wasn't
interested in the church,

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:25.304
I was interested in the girl.

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:27.139 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I figured if I was ever
going to see her again,

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:30.009
I couldn't tell them
what I really believed.

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:32.645 align:start size:97% position:3%
But at the end of that day,
I was really intrigued,

00:08:32.645 --> 00:08:35.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was captured by
the message that I heard.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.616 line:0%
And I began investigating,

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:39.051 line:0%
and eventually came to
the conclusion that maybe

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:40.286 line:0%
this isn't all an accident,

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:42.054 line:0%
and maybe I don't
know everything,

00:08:42.054 --> 00:08:44.257
and eventually became persuaded

00:08:44.257 --> 00:08:46.225
that the message of the Gospel

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:48.828
and the message in the Bible

00:08:48.828 --> 00:08:52.498 align:start size:97% position:3%
was one that I wanted to
embrace with all of my heart.

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:54.066
And I began going that way,

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:58.104 align:start position:0%
and it really changed my
trajectory, not only personally,

00:08:58.104 --> 00:09:02.475
but I wanted my personal
beliefs and convictions,

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:04.210
which I felt were were right,

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:06.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
to line up with the things
I did professionally

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:09.015
because I knew it would
influence other people.

00:09:09.015 --> 00:09:11.751
You know, kind of like
what I think you're doing

00:09:11.751 --> 00:09:13.619
a beautiful job of
taking the values

00:09:13.619 --> 00:09:16.489
that mean something to you
and helping to spread them

00:09:16.489 --> 00:09:20.092
because you want to produce,
you know, human flourishing.

00:09:20.092 --> 00:09:22.795 align:start size:88% position:13%
You don't want to squash
that with bad ideas,

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:25.298 align:start size:88% position:13%
but up uplift it and
help it with good ideas.

00:09:25.298 --> 00:09:28.401
- Were you surprised when you
started talking about that

00:09:28.401 --> 00:09:31.771
and doing some other shows and
doing some stuff on your own?

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:34.373 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I assume you probably,
your agents must've been like,

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:35.908
"Oh no, he's going in this road.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:37.443
He's going down this road.

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:38.978
This ain't gonna fly."

00:09:38.978 --> 00:09:40.179
- Yeah.

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:41.981 align:start size:88% position:13%
Yeah, that kind of stuff
did start to happen.

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:45.117 align:start size:88% position:13%
And, you know, really
it was, I mean, imagine,

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:48.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm 17, imagine you,
David, you're 17 years old,

00:09:48.287 --> 00:09:49.989
you're on a TV show.

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:52.058
I would rather be playing
basketball with my friends,

00:09:52.058 --> 00:09:54.493 align:start position:0%
but I got a huge
responsibility and kind of like

00:09:54.493 --> 00:09:57.029
whatever I do affects
all these other people

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:58.798
and their livelihood.

00:09:58.798 --> 00:10:01.701
And I'm feeling like, "Hey,
I think some of these jokes

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:05.404
for this family show in the
eighties is really kind of

00:10:05.404 --> 00:10:07.940
maybe sending kids
down the wrong road."

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:11.310 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so I would request
for a line change.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:14.714
Well, that could be seen
as flexing celebrity muscle

00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:17.383
from a 17 year old kid
who thinks he's all that

00:10:17.383 --> 00:10:20.286 align:start size:88% position:13%
when really, all I
wanted to do was be able

00:10:20.286 --> 00:10:22.254
to go to sleep at night
with a clear conscience.

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:24.724 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so people
started to get upset,

00:10:24.724 --> 00:10:27.259
and then all kinds of, you know,

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:29.495
E! Entertainment crazy
stories were coming out.

00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:30.963 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, "Kirk
Cameron born again,"

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:34.467 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Kirk Cameron tanks the
show," "Has actress fired."

00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:38.170 align:start size:84% position:16%
When in reality, that
wasn't it at all.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:42.141 align:start size:88% position:13%
And, you know, I look
back on "Growing Pains,"

00:10:42.141 --> 00:10:44.944
and I say there were ups and
downs, there was challenges,

00:10:44.944 --> 00:10:46.512 align:start size:84% position:16%
but ultimately, that's
where I found out

00:10:46.512 --> 00:10:48.047
who my true friends are,

00:10:48.047 --> 00:10:51.150
and that's where my faith in
God was actually strengthened

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.153
because it really caused
me to examine the things

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:58.157
that I hold dear and make
sure that they're tested

00:10:58.157 --> 00:10:59.825
and that they're true.

00:10:59.825 --> 00:11:02.962
- So as a guy that
grew up as a kid

00:11:02.962 --> 00:11:05.698
and as an atheist, I
suppose, on television,

00:11:05.698 --> 00:11:07.333
then you have your
kind of awakening,

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:11.671 align:start size:84% position:16%
does it surprise you
that Hollywood is
kind of where it's at

00:11:11.671 --> 00:11:14.740
at the moment, which I'm sure
most of my viewers will agree

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:16.676
is not a great place?

00:11:16.676 --> 00:11:17.543
- Does it surprise me?

00:11:17.543 --> 00:11:19.612
Well, you know,

00:11:19.612 --> 00:11:23.115 align:start size:97% position:3%
I guess I don't know whether
it surprises me or not.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.452 align:start size:84% position:16%
One of the things that
I find interesting

00:11:26.452 --> 00:11:29.789
is that when people are afraid

00:11:29.789 --> 00:11:33.826 align:start size:97% position:3%
of public shame or
humiliation or condemnation,

00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:35.061
we don't like that, right,

00:11:35.061 --> 00:11:36.662
and so we tend to like hide,

00:11:36.662 --> 00:11:39.031 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we don't let
people see who we are

00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:40.232
or really what we believe.

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:41.567
And I think unfortunately,

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:43.402
people within the
family of faith

00:11:43.402 --> 00:11:47.206
have felt that way and sort of
kept that stuff under wraps,

00:11:47.206 --> 00:11:51.977
even though the world is
increasingly religious.

00:11:51.977 --> 00:11:54.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
I believe that were
actually designed to know

00:11:54.747 --> 00:11:58.784
and to love God, and so we
wind up worshiping something

00:11:58.784 --> 00:12:00.052
if it's not God.

00:12:00.052 --> 00:12:01.854
Whether it's yourself,
or it's the government,

00:12:01.854 --> 00:12:04.457
or it's a group of people
you think are smarter,

00:12:04.457 --> 00:12:09.462
But ultimately from that
source will come our laws,

00:12:10.329 --> 00:12:11.263
and it will dictate our morality

00:12:11.263 --> 00:12:12.631
and all of that kind of thing.

00:12:12.631 --> 00:12:16.235
I hope that people of
faith will begin to

00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:20.706
not divorce that faith from
the arts and entertainment.

00:12:20.706 --> 00:12:22.708 align:start size:97% position:3%
I hope that they'll take
their faith and their values

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.844
and let it permeate the things

00:12:24.844 --> 00:12:26.746 align:start size:81% position:19%
that will then
shape the culture.

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:30.015
And I think when we see more
and more faith-based movies

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:32.151 align:start size:88% position:13%
doing better and better
at the box office,

00:12:32.151 --> 00:12:34.587
you look at "The Chosen," and
you see how well that's doing.

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:36.088
You look at the quality of that.

00:12:36.088 --> 00:12:37.289
You look at "The Passion
of the Christ" years ago,

00:12:37.289 --> 00:12:39.325
And even the movie
that I just finished.

00:12:40.526 --> 00:12:43.129
I think that people are
beginning to say, like,

00:12:43.129 --> 00:12:44.363
Wait a minute.

00:12:44.363 --> 00:12:45.731
There's not only
a market for this,

00:12:45.731 --> 00:12:48.167 align:start size:97% position:3%
but this is actually
communicating good messages,"

00:12:48.167 --> 00:12:49.935
that most of us, I
believe in America,

00:12:49.935 --> 00:12:51.470
understand we're
getting away from,

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.139
and we want to get
back to those things.

00:12:53.139 --> 00:12:56.008 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I'm hoping for a
revival, not just, you know,

00:12:56.008 --> 00:12:58.744
in the heart of people of faith,

00:12:58.744 --> 00:13:02.348 align:start size:84% position:16%
but in Hollywood and
in government and
in the marketplace

00:13:02.348 --> 00:13:03.582
and everywhere else.

00:13:03.582 --> 00:13:05.484
- Are you hopeful Just
because of how crazy

00:13:05.484 --> 00:13:06.852
the last year and a half was?

00:13:06.852 --> 00:13:08.287
I've sort of come around to that

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:10.790 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I think so many
people, you know,

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:12.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
yeah, people are
depressed, they're angry,

00:13:12.758 --> 00:13:14.493
they're confused,
all of that stuff,

00:13:14.493 --> 00:13:18.330
but it caused them to look at
their lives more seriously,

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.065
and so I'm hopeful for that.

00:13:20.966 --> 00:13:22.468
- Yeah, I think you're right.

00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:25.771
And I think that they've, at
the end of the day, you know,

00:13:25.771 --> 00:13:27.673
if you and I jump
off a building,

00:13:29.775 --> 00:13:32.444 align:start size:81% position:19%
we don't break the
law of gravity;

00:13:32.444 --> 00:13:35.080
the law of gravity breaks us.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.149 align:start size:88% position:13%
There are things that
are built into the world

00:13:37.149 --> 00:13:38.651
that are non-negotiables.

00:13:38.651 --> 00:13:41.487 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that false systems
will always end up failing.

00:13:41.487 --> 00:13:43.889 align:start size:97% position:3%
They may flourish for a
while, but it's kind of like

00:13:43.889 --> 00:13:46.425
that big tree that you
see in the background.

00:13:46.425 --> 00:13:49.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes, you know,
these Oak trees get so big

00:13:49.028 --> 00:13:52.598 align:start size:97% position:3%
and top heavy with all their
big, impressive branches,

00:13:52.598 --> 00:13:56.068 align:start position:0%
but if the root system
underneath is not as developed,

00:13:56.068 --> 00:13:58.804
if it's not down deep, all
it takes is a strong wind,

00:13:58.804 --> 00:14:02.041
and the thing topples itself
'úcause it's way too top heavy.

00:14:02.041 --> 00:14:04.944
And I think our culture
is getting that way.

00:14:04.944 --> 00:14:07.513 align:start size:84% position:16%
Eventually it will
teeter and topple over

00:14:07.513 --> 00:14:11.183
because our foundational
roots of faith and morality

00:14:11.183 --> 00:14:12.818
and virtue that
our founders said

00:14:12.818 --> 00:14:15.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
were absolutely essential
for a free society

00:14:15.187 --> 00:14:18.090
have begun to rot and
we've neglected them.

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:19.391
So if we see rotten fruit,

00:14:19.391 --> 00:14:22.061
culturally, I think
that the real answer

00:14:22.061 --> 00:14:25.130
is a systemic answer,
and we need to go down,

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:27.700
and we need to begin to re
nourish the roots again.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.401 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So you're sort of
answering my next question,

00:14:29.401 --> 00:14:31.403 align:start size:97% position:3%
but how does the faith part-
- I knew that.

00:14:31.403 --> 00:14:33.239 align:start size:88% position:13%
- That was pretty good,
what you did there.

00:14:33.239 --> 00:14:35.674
How does the faith part get
you to that flag behind you

00:14:35.674 --> 00:14:39.411
and sort of shape what
you believe politically?

00:14:39.411 --> 00:14:41.313
- Yeah, well, I've never,

00:14:41.313 --> 00:14:42.748
I'm really not a political guy.

00:14:42.748 --> 00:14:44.083
I'm a family guy.

00:14:44.083 --> 00:14:45.651
I would say I'm a faith guy.

00:14:46.986 --> 00:14:50.489 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I have kids in the
world, and I think to myself,

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:52.858
what's the place going
to be like in 20 years?

00:14:52.858 --> 00:14:54.560
That's a terrifying question

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.529
when I think about where
we're headed right now

00:14:57.529 --> 00:14:59.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
politically, economically,
morally spiritually.

00:14:59.865 --> 00:15:01.901
That's why I'm glad
for your program.

00:15:01.901 --> 00:15:06.238
I'm glad for many others who
are communicating this message.

00:15:06.238 --> 00:15:08.908
And so what I did is I said,

00:15:08.908 --> 00:15:10.075
"You know what?

00:15:10.075 --> 00:15:11.510
Guys like George Washington,

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:16.482 align:start size:97% position:3%
people like Abraham Lincoln,
and the pilgrims even

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:21.921 align:start size:97% position:3%
said that faith and morality
are absolute essential

00:15:22.788 --> 00:15:24.256
for a free and just society."

00:15:24.256 --> 00:15:25.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I began researching
and educating myself,

00:15:25.691 --> 00:15:28.794 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I found that the people
who built this country

00:15:29.895 --> 00:15:32.031 align:start size:88% position:13%
did something that
we're not doing anymore,

00:15:32.031 --> 00:15:35.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that is they're making
these sacred promises

00:15:35.901 --> 00:15:38.804
with one another to
covenant together.

00:15:38.804 --> 00:15:40.906
It's not just a legal contract

00:15:40.906 --> 00:15:43.742
that we can show to a judge
later when somebody screws up

00:15:43.742 --> 00:15:47.413 align:start size:84% position:16%
and, you know,
breaks the contract.

00:15:47.413 --> 00:15:50.382
But it's this sense that
'til death do us part,

00:15:50.382 --> 00:15:52.952
we are going to have
each other's back,

00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:54.553
and we're going to do the
right thing from the heart,

00:15:54.553 --> 00:15:57.423 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we're going to
promise with God as well

00:15:57.423 --> 00:16:00.059
that if he would protect
us, if he would guide us,

00:16:00.059 --> 00:16:04.196
that we trust and believe
that things will go well.

00:16:04.196 --> 00:16:05.264
And our forefathers did that,

00:16:05.264 --> 00:16:06.999
our foremothers understood that.

00:16:06.999 --> 00:16:08.801 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's what they
taught to their kids.

00:16:08.801 --> 00:16:11.437
And I believe that we
need to go back to that

00:16:11.437 --> 00:16:13.172
if we want to see
America flourish

00:16:13.172 --> 00:16:14.907
as a free and just society.

00:16:14.907 --> 00:16:17.843
Even economically,
even educationally,

00:16:17.843 --> 00:16:22.614 align:start size:97% position:3%
all of these things, I think
are our fruit on the tree

00:16:22.614 --> 00:16:27.619
with the roots going down
into faith and virtue.

00:16:29.021 --> 00:16:31.590
And that's what I'm trying
to get people to think about,

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.959
hoping that we, the
people of America,

00:16:33.959 --> 00:16:35.461
will come up with a solution

00:16:35.461 --> 00:16:38.630
and not wait for our hope
to fly in on Air Force One.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:39.798
- It ain't coming.

00:16:39.798 --> 00:16:41.567
Not from any Air Force One,

00:16:41.567 --> 00:16:44.570
but particularly not from the
guy on this Air Force One.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:46.271
Which one of your
sons did I meet?

00:16:46.271 --> 00:16:47.506
How old was he?

00:16:47.506 --> 00:16:50.109
- So that's James,
and James is 18,

00:16:50.109 --> 00:16:53.112 align:start size:88% position:13%
and he actually took his
last math final today

00:16:53.112 --> 00:16:55.447
and graduated high school.

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:56.482 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Wow.
- Very exciting day.

00:16:56.482 --> 00:16:57.950 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Do I say
congratulations to you?

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.118
I guess so.

00:16:59.118 --> 00:17:00.085
You're the dad, you got...

00:17:00.085 --> 00:17:01.153
- Yeah, thanks.

00:17:01.153 --> 00:17:02.354
Thanks, yeah.

00:17:02.354 --> 00:17:03.589
- Tell James I said
congratulations.

00:17:03.589 --> 00:17:04.790
But the reason I bring him up

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.892
is because I met you
at an event in Florida.

00:17:06.892 --> 00:17:08.460 align:start size:84% position:16%
A bunch of his friends
were around there,

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.828
and you were saying,
"Oh, Dave, you know,

00:17:09.828 --> 00:17:12.164
you've affected these kids."

00:17:12.164 --> 00:17:13.632 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I love hearing
that because it's like,

00:17:13.632 --> 00:17:15.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
oh, that means that
there are young people

00:17:15.401 --> 00:17:17.202
who are thinking about freedom,

00:17:17.202 --> 00:17:19.371
thinking about all the
things that I talk about.

00:17:19.371 --> 00:17:20.906
Are you hopeful,

00:17:20.906 --> 00:17:22.908 align:start size:88% position:13%
like when you talk to
your kids of those ages,

00:17:22.908 --> 00:17:25.978
who are going to be the ones
that get us out of this mess,

00:17:25.978 --> 00:17:28.680
like, are you hopeful
that they can do it?

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:29.948
- Yeah, I am hopeful
that they can do it.

00:17:29.948 --> 00:17:32.651
It's always young
people that have,

00:17:32.651 --> 00:17:34.186
that they're frontal...

00:17:34.186 --> 00:17:38.924
Well, A, they have all of this
energy, all of this passion,

00:17:38.924 --> 00:17:40.592 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they want to change
the world, right?

00:17:40.592 --> 00:17:42.728
I mean, you talk
about young people

00:17:42.728 --> 00:17:45.631
and always talking about
they want cultural change,

00:17:45.631 --> 00:17:47.332
they want a revolution,
and they want to be part

00:17:47.332 --> 00:17:49.601
of something bigger
than themselves.

00:17:49.601 --> 00:17:52.604
A lot of the older
folks, I'm 50 now,

00:17:52.604 --> 00:17:56.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
we have gray hair, which
is a sign of wisdom.

00:17:56.175 --> 00:17:57.609
We've been around a while to see

00:17:57.609 --> 00:18:00.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
that all this history stuff
is actually important.

00:18:00.879 --> 00:18:04.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so when you're
young, you need a vision.

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:08.720
And so I think that
if we give the vision

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:10.155
as older wiser people

00:18:10.155 --> 00:18:12.825 align:start size:88% position:13%
who understand that
ideas have consequences,

00:18:12.825 --> 00:18:15.260
that history can teach us about

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.995 align:start size:81% position:19%
where we're headed
in the future,

00:18:16.995 --> 00:18:19.031
that if they get
on board with that

00:18:19.031 --> 00:18:20.666
and they're inspired,

00:18:20.666 --> 00:18:25.671 align:start position:0%
if they catch the vision that's
rooted in the right stuff,

00:18:26.538 --> 00:18:28.841
I think that that not only,

00:18:28.841 --> 00:18:30.275
I don't think that it's they

00:18:30.275 --> 00:18:31.944 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are going to
make the difference,

00:18:31.944 --> 00:18:36.014
I'm banking on the power of
God working in their hearts

00:18:36.014 --> 00:18:39.184
and through their minds
to make better decisions

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:41.620
than we've made in
this generation.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.188
That's where my hope is.

00:18:43.188 --> 00:18:45.591
- What have you done, you
and your wife, I guess,

00:18:45.591 --> 00:18:47.860 align:start size:84% position:16%
to make sure your
kids are not infected

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.795
by so much of what's
going on out there

00:18:49.795 --> 00:18:52.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
with critical race
theory, identity politics,

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:53.632
just all the cultural norms?

00:18:53.632 --> 00:18:55.801
Because I get a ton of
questions about that

00:18:55.801 --> 00:18:58.770
from people that are of
our old age, 45 and 50,

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:01.240
that are like, "What do
I do about the kids?"

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.641
- Yeah.

00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:06.445 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, that's a great question,
and I don't have the,

00:19:06.445 --> 00:19:09.348 align:start position:0%
I don't know, that I have a
one size fits all fix for that,

00:19:09.348 --> 00:19:12.851 align:start size:97% position:3%
but, you know. we homeschooled
our kids for many years,

00:19:12.851 --> 00:19:14.052
and we didn't do that

00:19:14.052 --> 00:19:15.521
because we were running
away from something.

00:19:15.521 --> 00:19:19.324 align:start position:0%
We felt we could offer our kids
a superior educational path

00:19:19.324 --> 00:19:20.993
by teaching them the values

00:19:20.993 --> 00:19:23.795 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and giving them the
sources of information

00:19:23.795 --> 00:19:27.065 line:0%
and history about,
and government and
literature and faith

00:19:27.065 --> 00:19:30.169 line:0%
that they weren't going to
get at a regular school.

00:19:30.169 --> 00:19:32.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then some of the
years were actually spent

00:19:32.838 --> 00:19:34.439
at private schools as well.

00:19:34.439 --> 00:19:37.843
But this stuff that you're
talking about is pervasive.

00:19:37.843 --> 00:19:39.711
And so, you know, honestly,

00:19:39.711 --> 00:19:43.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
I invite friends, my kids'
friends and my friends,

00:19:43.782 --> 00:19:45.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
to sit around a
campfire like this,

00:19:45.751 --> 00:19:47.486
and to say, "Hey what do
you think of that flag?"

00:19:47.486 --> 00:19:49.688
You know, "What is
important to you?"

00:19:49.688 --> 00:19:50.923
"What are you kids,

00:19:50.923 --> 00:19:52.658
what are your friends
dealing with right now,

00:19:52.658 --> 00:19:55.093 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, in relationships,
politically?"

00:19:55.093 --> 00:19:57.129
You know, "What are
the taboo things

00:19:57.129 --> 00:19:58.463
that you can and cannot say?"

00:19:58.463 --> 00:20:00.199 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then we discuss
those things.

00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:03.402 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think not just
swallowing the narrative

00:20:03.402 --> 00:20:06.772
that's coming in off of
your social media feed,

00:20:06.772 --> 00:20:09.274
but researching things,

00:20:09.274 --> 00:20:11.610 align:start size:97% position:3%
and that's even becoming
increasingly difficult, right?

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:13.378
Because stuff's getting
scrubbed off the internet

00:20:13.378 --> 00:20:15.380
and filtered out
to where, you know,

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:17.249 align:start size:88% position:13%
I can't even say
certain words right now.

00:20:17.249 --> 00:20:19.418
You and I I might get
this video scrubbed.

00:20:19.418 --> 00:20:23.188 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so maybe you
found a workaround,
but it's challenging.

00:20:23.188 --> 00:20:25.524
- Well, yeah, last
week, I had to edit

00:20:25.524 --> 00:20:28.193
for the first time ever in
all my years of doing a show.

00:20:28.193 --> 00:20:29.127
- Really?

00:20:29.127 --> 00:20:30.362
- We had David Horowitz on.

00:20:30.362 --> 00:20:32.197
He said something
that he believed

00:20:32.197 --> 00:20:34.733
as a free person in a
somewhat free society.

00:20:34.733 --> 00:20:37.202
But we knew that if
we aired it as is,

00:20:37.202 --> 00:20:38.670
we were going to get,

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were in risk of getting
our channel booted.

00:20:40.205 --> 00:20:43.075
For the first time ever,
I had to edit something,

00:20:43.075 --> 00:20:46.278
or we put soundbars
over it on YouTube.

00:20:46.278 --> 00:20:47.879
Put it on my Locals
channel, though.

00:20:47.879 --> 00:20:48.814
- Yeah.

00:20:48.814 --> 00:20:49.781
Well, that's great.

00:20:49.781 --> 00:20:50.749
And you know what I hope Dave

00:20:50.749 --> 00:20:54.152
is I hope that we realize like,

00:20:55.587 --> 00:20:57.689 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, that we're all sort
of kicking ourselves now,

00:20:57.689 --> 00:20:59.224 align:start size:84% position:16%
going, "Wait a
minute, wait a minute.

00:20:59.224 --> 00:21:01.393
Why did we think of creating
our own social media channels

00:21:01.393 --> 00:21:04.129
and news outlets and
keeping those free?

00:21:04.129 --> 00:21:06.565
Why don't we think of
that 40 years ago?"

00:21:06.565 --> 00:21:08.934 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, but the good
news, I think now,

00:21:08.934 --> 00:21:10.369
is we're waking up to it,

00:21:10.369 --> 00:21:13.038
and now these things are
beginning to be formed,

00:21:13.038 --> 00:21:15.440
and now we're beginning
to be able to, you know,

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:19.344
not rely on other
people who disagree

00:21:19.344 --> 00:21:21.246
and want to squash our message

00:21:21.246 --> 00:21:23.015 align:start size:84% position:16%
to distribute and
promote our message.

00:21:23.015 --> 00:21:24.483
That just doesn't make sense,

00:21:24.483 --> 00:21:26.585
but, you know, it was
easy, it was free,

00:21:26.585 --> 00:21:29.855
and so we just kinda
went along with it.

00:21:29.855 --> 00:21:33.025
So I'm hopeful that we are
at a very exciting point

00:21:33.025 --> 00:21:35.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
in history and that
people are gonna look back

00:21:35.527 --> 00:21:37.529
on this generation and say

00:21:37.529 --> 00:21:42.534 align:start size:97% position:3%
there were a few people they
may have been, you know,

00:21:43.568 --> 00:21:45.137
out funded and outnumbered,

00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:48.173
but they did the right thing
and Heaven was behind them,

00:21:48.173 --> 00:21:49.474
and they made the difference.

00:21:49.474 --> 00:21:52.110
- That guy, David,
beat Goliath, right?

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:53.679
Am I getting that story correct?

00:21:54.746 --> 00:21:56.014
- He did.

00:21:56.014 --> 00:21:57.282
But you know, he
was a little guy,

00:21:57.282 --> 00:21:58.817
and David was a really big guy.

00:21:58.817 --> 00:22:02.154
And I think the lesson
there is that, you know,

00:22:02.154 --> 00:22:04.790
the only way that that
story ever makes sense

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:08.660 align:start size:97% position:3%
is when God is working through
David to defeat Goliath.

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:11.363
And that's my hope is that
he'll also work through us

00:22:11.363 --> 00:22:15.701
to take down the
nefarious forces

00:22:15.701 --> 00:22:17.369
that would love to
see freedom go away.

00:22:17.369 --> 00:22:19.938
- So for the people
that have not seen

00:22:19.938 --> 00:22:21.173
the "Campfire Revival,"

00:22:21.173 --> 00:22:23.342 align:start size:84% position:16%
you are sitting at the
campfire right now.

00:22:23.342 --> 00:22:24.910
You lit the fire for us.

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:27.179
Hopefully you're not
going to self-immolate

00:22:27.179 --> 00:22:29.114
or burn the flag
while we're here.

00:22:29.114 --> 00:22:31.883
But you did this all
just as we sat down.

00:22:31.883 --> 00:22:34.953 align:start size:97% position:3%
What are you doing over there
at the "Campfire Revival"

00:22:34.953 --> 00:22:37.456
on Instagram and Facebook?

00:22:37.456 --> 00:22:39.157
Is that it, just chat?

00:22:39.157 --> 00:22:40.192
Well, I know what you're doing.

00:22:40.192 --> 00:22:41.793
So I'm asking you,

00:22:41.793 --> 00:22:43.628 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm asking as the
audience, not as myself.

00:22:43.628 --> 00:22:44.863
I know what you're doing.

00:22:44.863 --> 00:22:48.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay, so basically,
this all started,

00:22:48.734 --> 00:22:51.069 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, after this
whole last year,

00:22:51.069 --> 00:22:53.972
and then through the election
time and then the inauguration

00:22:53.972 --> 00:22:55.674 align:start size:97% position:3%
and people are talking
about the first hundred days

00:22:55.674 --> 00:22:56.942
of the administration,

00:22:56.942 --> 00:22:59.411
and, you know, so many
of us have been sort of

00:22:59.411 --> 00:23:02.647
like waiting and hoping for
someone else to do something,

00:23:02.647 --> 00:23:04.149
and we're waiting
for this to happen.

00:23:04.149 --> 00:23:06.284
And I thought to myself, as
I'm sitting in my backyard

00:23:06.284 --> 00:23:08.520
cooped up in the California,

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:11.523 align:start size:84% position:16%
where you're basically
under house arrest

00:23:11.523 --> 00:23:14.059
and lockdown at the time,

00:23:14.059 --> 00:23:16.294
"Wait a minute, what's our plan?

00:23:16.294 --> 00:23:21.299
What kind of a hundred day
plan could I be a part of

00:23:22.701 --> 00:23:24.035
that's going to actually
promote the positive change

00:23:24.035 --> 00:23:26.037 align:start size:97% position:3%
rather than just
complaining about the things

00:23:26.037 --> 00:23:27.105
that I don't like to see?"

00:23:27.105 --> 00:23:28.807
And I said, "You know what?

00:23:28.807 --> 00:23:30.275
I don't know the best plan,

00:23:30.275 --> 00:23:32.444
but I'm going to start a
plan, and it's going to be,

00:23:32.444 --> 00:23:34.880 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm going to sit in my
backyard for 100 days in a row

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:37.015
and build a campfire."

00:23:37.015 --> 00:23:39.151
And I'm going to invite
other people to join me

00:23:39.151 --> 00:23:42.020
as we pray, as we worship God,

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:44.256 align:start size:88% position:13%
and as we begin to
learn what made America

00:23:44.256 --> 00:23:46.725 align:start position:0%
the freest, strongest, most
prosperous nation in the world.

00:23:46.725 --> 00:23:49.895
And we found that
on Facebook Live,

00:23:49.895 --> 00:23:54.433
we'd have 15 to 20,000 people
every single night joining,

00:23:54.433 --> 00:23:55.901
and the comments were flying,

00:23:55.901 --> 00:23:57.936
and people made it a
destination every night

00:23:57.936 --> 00:24:00.972
because they found hope
and they found something

00:24:00.972 --> 00:24:03.508 align:start size:84% position:16%
for them to talk
about with their kids.

00:24:03.508 --> 00:24:05.544
And we did that for 100 days,

00:24:05.544 --> 00:24:07.612 align:start size:88% position:13%
called it the "American
Campfire Revival."

00:24:07.612 --> 00:24:10.382
And it's all about that
inside out strategy,

00:24:10.382 --> 00:24:13.585 align:start size:97% position:3%
that bottom up strategy
that our founders understood

00:24:13.585 --> 00:24:16.021 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that I think is
going to be the solution

00:24:16.021 --> 00:24:17.689
to getting us back to
where we want to go.

00:24:17.689 --> 00:24:18.890
- Yeah.

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:20.125 align:start size:84% position:16%
What else are you
working on right now?

00:24:20.125 --> 00:24:21.393
Are you going to
be traveling again

00:24:21.393 --> 00:24:23.261
and spreading the word
and getting out there?

00:24:23.261 --> 00:24:24.930
I mean, you're hear in Cali,

00:24:24.930 --> 00:24:27.833
where we are opening up
apparently at some point.

00:24:27.833 --> 00:24:30.769
- Yeah, that's right.

00:24:30.769 --> 00:24:33.238
Well, I am working on
quite a few things.

00:24:33.238 --> 00:24:35.807 align:start size:88% position:13%
This "American Campfire
Revival" has been

00:24:35.807 --> 00:24:38.543 align:start size:88% position:13%
just kind of a surprise
joy for me to do.

00:24:38.543 --> 00:24:40.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
Although, all of my
wardrobe smells like smoke

00:24:40.712 --> 00:24:42.447 align:start size:84% position:16%
and my wife is kind
of tired of it.

00:24:42.447 --> 00:24:45.083 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm roasting like a
marshmallow as we speak.

00:24:45.083 --> 00:24:47.953 align:start size:84% position:16%
My backside is
turning golden brown.

00:24:47.953 --> 00:24:48.787
You just can't see it.

00:24:48.787 --> 00:24:50.222
- [Dave] Nice, nice.

00:24:51.423 --> 00:24:53.425
- And we're going
to continue this,

00:24:53.425 --> 00:24:56.027 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I'm about to
start another 40 days

00:24:56.027 --> 00:24:58.430
of the "American
Campfire Revival,"

00:24:58.430 --> 00:25:00.532
speaking about family covenants

00:25:00.532 --> 00:25:02.667 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then community
covenants, church covenants,

00:25:02.667 --> 00:25:04.269
and civil government covenants,

00:25:04.269 --> 00:25:06.438 align:start size:84% position:16%
that kind of all
weave together to form

00:25:06.438 --> 00:25:11.276 align:start position:0%
kind of this this Kevlar fabric
that I believe will resist

00:25:11.276 --> 00:25:14.913
the darts of tyranny
and totalitarianism.

00:25:14.913 --> 00:25:17.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fact, this is something
I wanted to show you.

00:25:17.849 --> 00:25:20.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
This is a pledge that
I kind of modeled

00:25:20.352 --> 00:25:22.120 align:start size:84% position:16%
after the "Declaration
of Independence,"

00:25:22.120 --> 00:25:24.756 align:start size:97% position:3%
called, "Our Pledge to Renew
the American Covenant."

00:25:24.756 --> 00:25:27.292 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's what we can
affirm together as families

00:25:27.292 --> 00:25:29.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
and as individuals to
get back to these values,

00:25:29.861 --> 00:25:32.464
and we've signed it here,

00:25:32.464 --> 00:25:34.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm hoping people
will hang us in their wall

00:25:34.399 --> 00:25:37.235 align:start size:97% position:3%
and talk about it as a family
and with their neighbors.

00:25:37.235 --> 00:25:39.538
And then we have some live
events around the country

00:25:39.538 --> 00:25:40.906
where we gather in
fields and farms...

00:25:40.906 --> 00:25:42.107
(loud popping noise)

00:25:42.107 --> 00:25:43.141
- Oh, whoa.

00:25:43.141 --> 00:25:44.709
You didn't just...

00:25:44.709 --> 00:25:45.610
- No, that's alright.

00:25:45.610 --> 00:25:46.444
We're good.

00:25:46.444 --> 00:25:47.679
We're good.

00:25:47.679 --> 00:25:48.847
- But if you dropped
the whole covenant

00:25:48.847 --> 00:25:49.548 align:start size:84% position:16%
in the fire just
then, that woulda'...

00:25:49.548 --> 00:25:50.382
- Here it is.

00:25:50.382 --> 00:25:51.416
And we're still good.

00:25:52.751 --> 00:25:55.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
And gather around
bonfires and sing and pray

00:25:55.287 --> 00:25:57.122 align:start size:84% position:16%
and talk about what
really matters,

00:25:57.122 --> 00:25:59.357
and if we have one
here in California,

00:25:59.357 --> 00:26:00.825 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'll make sure
that I invite you.

00:26:00.825 --> 00:26:01.760
I'd love to have you come.

00:26:01.760 --> 00:26:03.028
- I'd love to come.

00:26:03.028 --> 00:26:03.862
For a second, I thought
Newsome was about to try

00:26:03.862 --> 00:26:04.796
to take you out.

00:26:04.796 --> 00:26:06.064
I thought he had, you know,

00:26:06.064 --> 00:26:07.299
'cause he's got these
snipers out there.

00:26:07.299 --> 00:26:08.767
People are in the
backyard having fun

00:26:08.767 --> 00:26:10.669
with an American flag, jeez.

00:26:10.669 --> 00:26:12.537 align:start size:97% position:3%
- That's actually the
first time that's happened.

00:26:12.537 --> 00:26:16.107
So I think, if you see any
smoke coming from behind me,

00:26:16.107 --> 00:26:17.409
you let me know, okay?

00:26:17.409 --> 00:26:18.777
- Yeah, yeah.

00:26:18.777 --> 00:26:20.045 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I hope you have
insurance for this program.

00:26:20.045 --> 00:26:21.313
Wait, so give me some of the,

00:26:21.313 --> 00:26:25.083
give me two or three
of the, not edicts,

00:26:25.083 --> 00:26:27.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the principles that
are on the document there.

00:26:27.185 --> 00:26:28.019
- Oh yeah.

00:26:28.019 --> 00:26:28.887
- Yeah

00:26:28.887 --> 00:26:29.721
- That's it.

00:26:30.855 --> 00:26:31.890
Let's see.

00:26:34.926 --> 00:26:36.194
Boy, here we go.

00:26:36.194 --> 00:26:38.330
We promise to each
other as a family

00:26:38.330 --> 00:26:42.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
to provide for one
another as long as we live

00:26:42.167 --> 00:26:43.768
as commanded in scripture.

00:26:43.768 --> 00:26:45.470
There's so many others.

00:26:45.470 --> 00:26:46.504
We commit to living peacefully,

00:26:46.504 --> 00:26:47.939
to obeying the laws of the land

00:26:47.939 --> 00:26:51.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
and working to elect
godly, trustworthy leaders

00:26:51.276 --> 00:26:52.944
who will not abuse
their limited power

00:26:52.944 --> 00:26:55.714
as our public servants and
distort our constitution.

00:26:55.714 --> 00:26:59.284 align:start position:0%
So we talk about the civic
realm and also the family realm

00:26:59.284 --> 00:27:03.555
and also the community realm.

00:27:03.555 --> 00:27:06.391
And, you know, all
of it really begins

00:27:06.391 --> 00:27:07.592
with self-government, right?

00:27:07.592 --> 00:27:09.160
I think this is important.

00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:10.762
I think people would
find this interesting.

00:27:10.762 --> 00:27:12.731
When we talk about government,

00:27:12.731 --> 00:27:13.999 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're usually
talking about them,

00:27:13.999 --> 00:27:15.700
you know, like out
there or up there,

00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:18.470
we're talking about
the government and
what they're doing,

00:27:18.470 --> 00:27:22.474 align:start size:88% position:13%
but in our country,
our founders understood

00:27:22.474 --> 00:27:25.877 align:start size:97% position:3%
that that kind of
government will be terrible

00:27:25.877 --> 00:27:29.114
totalitarian government unless

00:27:30.649 --> 00:27:33.018
we lay the foundation
of self-government.

00:27:33.018 --> 00:27:36.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if we govern
ourselves according to the

00:27:36.388 --> 00:27:38.089
the rules of right, right,

00:27:38.089 --> 00:27:39.758 align:start size:84% position:16%
like, it's not
about left or right.

00:27:39.758 --> 00:27:41.059
It's about up or down.

00:27:41.059 --> 00:27:45.063 align:start size:88% position:13%
And if we go up to
Heaven's rules of right,

00:27:45.063 --> 00:27:48.199 align:start size:97% position:3%
then we don't need the
government with the big stick

00:27:48.199 --> 00:27:51.302
to beat us back into civility.

00:27:51.302 --> 00:27:52.303
We've already got that.

00:27:52.303 --> 00:27:53.772
We got that individually.

00:27:53.772 --> 00:27:54.806
We got it in our families.

00:27:54.806 --> 00:27:56.041
We got it in our communities,

00:27:56.041 --> 00:27:58.209 align:start size:84% position:16%
and government can
stay limited and small

00:27:58.209 --> 00:27:59.611
and people have freedom.

00:27:59.611 --> 00:28:02.247 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so that's
really the essence.

00:28:02.247 --> 00:28:06.251 align:start position:0%
The most powerful culture
transforming force in the world

00:28:06.251 --> 00:28:08.586
is the self-governing person

00:28:08.586 --> 00:28:11.823 align:start size:84% position:16%
who loves God and
loves their neighbor.

00:28:11.823 --> 00:28:13.358 align:start size:81% position:19%
That's what our
founders believed,

00:28:13.358 --> 00:28:16.327
and that's what I'm trying
to communicate to people.

00:28:16.327 --> 00:28:18.630 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Which one do you
think is harder

00:28:18.630 --> 00:28:21.032 align:start size:84% position:16%
for your old Hollywood
friends to swallow:

00:28:21.032 --> 00:28:24.135 align:start position:0%
the belief part or your
feelings about government part?

00:28:24.135 --> 00:28:27.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because they probably
not thrilled with either.

00:28:27.172 --> 00:28:28.673
(Kirk laughing)

00:28:28.673 --> 00:28:30.575 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You mean government
being limited?

00:28:30.575 --> 00:28:32.377 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, well, that you
believe in small government

00:28:32.377 --> 00:28:34.579
and the constitution, that
America is good, you know,

00:28:34.579 --> 00:28:36.114
that sort of stuff,

00:28:36.114 --> 00:28:38.950
or the belief part, is that
harder for them to swallow?

00:28:41.186 --> 00:28:42.020
- Oh boy.

00:28:43.855 --> 00:28:45.123
I dunno.

00:28:45.123 --> 00:28:46.191
You know, it's all
so tied together.

00:28:46.191 --> 00:28:49.427
But actually, I think that

00:28:52.330 --> 00:28:53.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's interesting you said
that small government

00:28:53.832 --> 00:28:55.467
and that America is good.

00:28:55.467 --> 00:28:57.102
You know, the principles...

00:28:57.102 --> 00:28:58.303
- [Dave] Radical stuff, I know.

00:28:58.303 --> 00:29:00.405
- Is founded on are
absolutely good.

00:29:00.405 --> 00:29:01.940
The framework is genius.

00:29:01.940 --> 00:29:06.811
It's beautiful, but it depends
on personal self-government.

00:29:06.811 --> 00:29:08.713 align:start size:84% position:16%
All of our founders
told us that,

00:29:08.713 --> 00:29:11.516 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the truth is I'm
actually for big government,

00:29:11.516 --> 00:29:12.550
but it's not what you think.

00:29:12.550 --> 00:29:14.052
It's big self-government.

00:29:14.052 --> 00:29:16.121
It's big family government.

00:29:16.121 --> 00:29:18.389
And once we take care of that,

00:29:19.924 --> 00:29:22.193
we don't need a big police force

00:29:22.193 --> 00:29:23.862 align:start size:84% position:16%
because we're doing
the right thing

00:29:23.862 --> 00:29:26.097
at the friend and family level.

00:29:26.097 --> 00:29:27.932
- I think a lot of people
are watching this going,

00:29:27.932 --> 00:29:31.770 align:start size:97% position:3%
"What are you two fools
still doing in California?"

00:29:31.770 --> 00:29:35.440 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, at this point for
you, is it just the weather?

00:29:35.440 --> 00:29:39.310
I mean, you could be
doing this in Florida

00:29:39.310 --> 00:29:41.780
or Texas or Tennessee.

00:29:41.780 --> 00:29:42.614
- Yeah.

00:29:42.614 --> 00:29:44.082
Yeah, that's true.

00:29:44.082 --> 00:29:44.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I certainly understand
why people are moving

00:29:44.883 --> 00:29:46.351
out of here.

00:29:46.351 --> 00:29:47.752 align:start position:0%
They're getting out of here
like rats jumping off of a ship

00:29:47.752 --> 00:29:51.089 align:start size:97% position:3%
because we're sinking
economically and politically;

00:29:51.089 --> 00:29:54.259
however, I'm all about revival.

00:29:54.259 --> 00:29:56.394 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look at my shirt, "American
Campfire Revival."

00:29:56.394 --> 00:29:57.929
Revival, right?

00:29:57.929 --> 00:30:01.099
So that means, like, putting
life back into things again.

00:30:01.099 --> 00:30:05.336
Things that are flat-lining
and dying, reviving them.

00:30:05.336 --> 00:30:07.605
I think that can
happen anywhere.

00:30:07.605 --> 00:30:09.674 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think it can happen
in my marriage,

00:30:09.674 --> 00:30:11.009
if my marriage is flat-lining.

00:30:11.009 --> 00:30:13.344
I think it can happen in
my family, my community.

00:30:13.344 --> 00:30:15.446 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think it can
happen in our state.

00:30:15.446 --> 00:30:17.515
And so I'm hoping and
praying that America

00:30:17.515 --> 00:30:22.520
and starting with California
begins to see a a renewal,

00:30:23.855 --> 00:30:26.224 align:start size:97% position:3%
a revival, and a resurgence
of the kind of stuff

00:30:26.224 --> 00:30:29.828 align:start size:97% position:3%
that will cause human
flourishing, not human decay.

00:30:29.828 --> 00:30:33.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
- What do you think we can
do in this crazy state?

00:30:33.565 --> 00:30:36.935 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, you know, I'm
hanging on by a thread, man.

00:30:36.935 --> 00:30:38.069
- I know.

00:30:38.069 --> 00:30:39.070
I hear you.

00:30:39.070 --> 00:30:40.338
I'm here.

00:30:40.338 --> 00:30:41.506
Well, I'm starting
with a campfire.

00:30:41.506 --> 00:30:42.340
- Alright, alright.

00:30:42.340 --> 00:30:43.575
Fair enough.

00:30:43.575 --> 00:30:44.542
Alright, that's it.

00:30:44.542 --> 00:30:46.110
I'm coming to the campfire.

00:30:46.110 --> 00:30:49.180
- And I'm listening to you,
and I'm listening to others,

00:30:49.180 --> 00:30:52.684
and I believe that
there are people

00:30:52.684 --> 00:30:55.253
with more brilliant
ideas than I have

00:30:55.253 --> 00:30:59.324
that are going to help move
us in the right direction.

00:30:59.324 --> 00:31:02.627
And I continue to pray for them.

00:31:02.627 --> 00:31:05.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Do you find that people
across the country,

00:31:05.430 --> 00:31:06.631
when you're traveling,

00:31:06.631 --> 00:31:08.066
regardless of whether
you're red or blue

00:31:08.066 --> 00:31:10.935 align:start position:0%
or any of that stuff, that
people are pretty much the same?

00:31:12.704 --> 00:31:13.638
Uh-oh, uh-oh.

00:31:13.638 --> 00:31:14.539
What's going on behind you now?

00:31:16.174 --> 00:31:18.309 align:start size:84% position:16%
- That people are
pretty much the same.

00:31:18.309 --> 00:31:19.711
What do you mean?

00:31:19.711 --> 00:31:20.945 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like, regardless of whether
they're red or blue?

00:31:20.945 --> 00:31:22.247
- That if you can
really get to them,

00:31:22.247 --> 00:31:24.282
that the stuff that
you're talking about

00:31:24.282 --> 00:31:26.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
is sort of the stuff
that they really believe,

00:31:26.284 --> 00:31:28.820 align:start size:84% position:16%
some of them just
don't know it maybe.

00:31:28.820 --> 00:31:30.622
- You know, I think
that people want it.

00:31:30.622 --> 00:31:31.589
People want it.

00:31:31.589 --> 00:31:32.857
They want to have a good job.

00:31:32.857 --> 00:31:34.292
They want to be able to
put food on their table

00:31:34.292 --> 00:31:36.394
and provide for their family.

00:31:36.394 --> 00:31:38.496
They want to have
a sense of purpose

00:31:38.496 --> 00:31:40.932 align:start size:84% position:16%
like their life
counts for something.

00:31:40.932 --> 00:31:45.937 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think people have
been sold different recipes

00:31:47.105 --> 00:31:48.640 align:start size:81% position:19%
on how they're
going to get that.

00:31:48.640 --> 00:31:51.109
And so, you know, politically,

00:31:51.109 --> 00:31:53.544 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
you know, are you
going to have somebody

00:31:53.544 --> 00:31:55.480 line:0%
who's going to give
you those things

00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:58.416 line:0%
or give you the opportunity
to work for those things

00:31:58.416 --> 00:31:59.784 line:0%
and invest in those things?

00:31:59.784 --> 00:32:03.788
That's one aspect of it.

00:32:03.788 --> 00:32:04.989 align:start size:81% position:19%
But I think at the
end of the day,

00:32:04.989 --> 00:32:06.758 align:start size:84% position:16%
if we're talking about
values, you know,

00:32:06.758 --> 00:32:10.128
I've got friends who are on
the other side of the aisle,

00:32:10.128 --> 00:32:14.933 align:start size:97% position:3%
and, you know, they want
the same things that I want.

00:32:14.933 --> 00:32:18.503
I want an opportunity to
provide for my family.

00:32:18.503 --> 00:32:21.372
I want an opportunity to
be able to speak the truth

00:32:21.372 --> 00:32:23.007
and not be censored for it.

00:32:23.007 --> 00:32:25.476
I want an opportunity
to pursue happiness

00:32:25.476 --> 00:32:29.914
and not be restricted
and controlled and
thrown into a cage

00:32:29.914 --> 00:32:32.450
because somebody
disagrees with me.

00:32:32.450 --> 00:32:36.321 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think there's a very
specific way to go about that,

00:32:36.321 --> 00:32:38.356
and that's what I'm
trying to promote.

00:32:38.356 --> 00:32:39.557
- Yeah.

00:32:39.557 --> 00:32:40.758 align:start size:84% position:16%
When you get those
guys on the other side

00:32:40.758 --> 00:32:42.160 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the aisle to come
to the campfire,

00:32:42.160 --> 00:32:43.394
are they able to do it?

00:32:43.394 --> 00:32:44.696
'Cause that's what a
lot of my, let's say,

00:32:44.696 --> 00:32:46.931 align:start size:88% position:13%
conservative friends
are now struggling with.

00:32:46.931 --> 00:32:49.734 align:start position:0%
It's like, "Yeah, I'll have
that conversation with anybody,"

00:32:49.734 --> 00:32:50.868
but they don't seem to want

00:32:50.868 --> 00:32:52.337 align:start size:84% position:16%
to have that
conversation with us.

00:32:53.371 --> 00:32:54.539
- Yeah.

00:32:54.539 --> 00:32:56.341 align:start size:84% position:16%
I do know what
you're talking about.

00:32:57.775 --> 00:33:02.280 align:start size:97% position:3%
I hope I'm not just, you know,
parroting something here.

00:33:02.280 --> 00:33:04.215
I think I really do see

00:33:05.483 --> 00:33:10.021
some groups of people
really going after

00:33:10.021 --> 00:33:13.424
facts and data and statistics,

00:33:13.424 --> 00:33:16.127
and I see other groups of people

00:33:16.127 --> 00:33:18.696
that seem to not want to
talk about those things,

00:33:18.696 --> 00:33:23.067
but really pour on the
lighter fluid of emotion

00:33:23.067 --> 00:33:26.604 align:start size:84% position:16%
and sometimes not
deal with the issues.

00:33:26.604 --> 00:33:28.139 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm all about dealing
with the issues

00:33:28.139 --> 00:33:30.508
and understanding
what the facts are,

00:33:30.508 --> 00:33:33.011 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then let's work
together to solve problems.

00:33:33.011 --> 00:33:36.848
You know, I've got a family too,

00:33:36.848 --> 00:33:38.282
and I've got neighbors too,

00:33:38.282 --> 00:33:41.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
and rather than the
government taking my money

00:33:41.185 --> 00:33:45.923
to give to other people
in an inefficient way,

00:33:45.923 --> 00:33:49.293
I would rather keep my money
and have a heart of compassion

00:33:49.293 --> 00:33:52.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
that gets to know my
neighbor and help them out

00:33:52.096 --> 00:33:53.297
at the local level.

00:33:53.297 --> 00:33:54.832 align:start size:84% position:16%
I just think that's
more efficient.

00:33:54.832 --> 00:33:56.934
I think that's better, and
it develops relationships

00:33:56.934 --> 00:33:59.137 align:start size:84% position:16%
that cause communities
to flourish.

00:33:59.137 --> 00:34:01.072 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Where am I sending
the fine people?

00:34:01.072 --> 00:34:02.540
Just to kirkcameron.com?

00:34:02.540 --> 00:34:05.676
Because if I send them
to Facebook, I mean,

00:34:05.676 --> 00:34:09.647 align:start size:97% position:3%
